From 0f9875e3bb27f50463209f56284da1cadfc0289b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yan Zhao <yan.y.zhao@intel.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Jan 2025 17:58:26 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 64/98] KVM: x86: Make cpu_dirty_log_size a per-VM value

Make cpu_dirty_log_size (CPU's dirty log buffer size) a per-VM value and
set the per-VM cpu_dirty_log_size only for normal VMs when PML is enabled.
Do not set it for TDs.

Previously, cpu_dirty_log_size was a system-wide value in kvm_x86_ops for
all VMs. It was set to the PML buffer size when PML was enabled in VMX.
However, PML is not currently supported in basic TDX enabling for TDs
though PML remains available for normal VMs as long as the feature is
supported by hardware and enabled in VMX.

Make cpu_dirty_log_size a per-VM value to allow it to be PML buffer size
for normal VMs and 0 for TDs. This allows functions like
kvm_arch_sync_dirty_log() and kvm_mmu_update_cpu_dirty_logging() to get the
correct PML buffer size, determining if PML is supported and if it's
necessary to kick off vCPUs or request to update CPU dirty logging status
(turn on/off PML in VMCS).

