---
- Remove KVM_PRE_FAULT_MEMORY call to keep up with API changes

- Reinette: Move tdx_read_capabilities() from "KVM: selftests: TDX: Use
  KVM_TDX_CAPABILITIES to validate TDs' attribute configuration" into this
  patch since TD creation depends on it. Move Isaku's "Suggested-by" tag
  with it but drop Binbin's "Reviewed-by" tag since the patch changed
  significantly. All other signatures are the same with Ackerley Tng
  already recognized as co-developer of this patch.

- Reinette: Squash Isakus' contribution to follow qemu tdx_mask_cpuid() and
  tdx_adjust_cpuid() @ qemu/target/i386/kvm/tdx.c to initialize cpuid
  array.  Export __tdx_mask_cpuid_features() for test cases that
  compares cpuid result. Add Co-developed-by to give attribution.

- Reinette: Squash Isaku's change to mimic QEMU to filter cpuid array.
  Otherwise KVM_TDX_INIT_VM fails. Drop kvm_tdx_init_vm_cpuid_data cpuid
  entry that the TDX module doesn't set directly. This is a catch-up
  for the KVM_TDX_INIT_VM change. Without this change KVM_TDX_INIT_VM
  results in EINVAL.

- Reinette: Squash Rick's fixup of CPUID struct to match KVM.
  Add Co-developed-by to give attribution.

- Reinette: Squash Isaku's change to export arch.s_bit to guest code.
  The guest needs shared bit.  Although the guest can use
  TDG.VP.VEINFO.GET(), it bloats guest code.  It simplifies the guest code
  to export the bits.

- Reinette: Squash Rick's change to remove KVM_CAP_MAX_VCPUS enable,
  it is no longer required/supported.

- Reinette: Add snippet to changelog to describe the changes made to
  CPUID entries.

- Reinette: Remove "Change-Id:" tag.

- Reinette: Remove tdx_configure_memory_encryption() because its
  functionality is handled in kvm_init_vm_address_properties().

- Reinette: Fix checkpatch.pl issues: line length, extern prototypes
  should be avoided in .h files, typo, use a blank line after
  function/struct/union/enum declarations, lines should not end with a '(',
  rewrite NULL comparison, missing a blank line after declarations,
  alignment should match open parenthesis, braces {} are not necessary
  for single statement blocks, don't use multiple blank lines, multiple
  assignments should be avoided, prefer using the BIT macro. Also, remove
  kerneldoc (/**) markers where comments do not follow kerneldoc syntax.

- Reinette: checkpatch.pl warns:
      Macro argument reuse 's' - possible side-effects?
      Macro argument reuse 'range_begin' - possible side-effects?
      Macro argument reuse 'range_end' - possible side-effects?
  Instead of reworking macro, remove it because it is a duplicate of
  existing sparsebit_for_each_set_range() found in
  tools/testing/selftests/kvm/include/sparsebit.h

- Reinette: switch to reverse fir where practical

- Adrian: Refresh CPUID after KVM_TDX_INIT_VCPU

- Adrian: Add has_protected_regs flag to avoid IOCTLs that access registers
  because they now return an error

- Reinette: Add KVM_TDX_GET_CPUID to the TDX commands known to TDX
  selftests so that any TDX selftest can call tdx_ioctl() with TDX command
  ID KVM_TDX_GET_CPUID.

- Reinette: Some of the CPUID entries being modified, specifically leaf 0x7
  have more than one sub-leaf. The mask of CPUID features is only intended
  for sub-leaf 0. Ensure masking is only done on sub-leaf 0.

- Reinette: Use KVM_TDX_GET_CPUID as baseline for KVM_SET_CPUID2.
  KVM_TDX_GET_CPUID returns the CPUID bits of a configured TD that reflects
  the adjustments in support of TDX that was made to the KVM supported
  CPUID obtained via KVM_GET_SUPPORTED_CPUID before creating the TD. No
  need to repeat the adjustments made by tdx_mask_cpuid_features() during
  TD creation that are already reflected in output of KVM_TDX_GET_CPUID.
  Remove tdx_adjust_cpuid() that sets CPUID bits hardcoded by TDX. CPUID
  bits returned by KVM_TDX_GET_CPUID already reflects this.
