Date: Tue, 25 Jun 2024 01:17:30 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 79/98] KVM: selftests: TDX: Add basic TDX CPUID test

The test reads CPUID values from inside a TD VM and compare them
to expected values.

The test targets CPUID values which are virtualized as "As Configured",
"As Configured (if Native)", "Calculated", "Fixed" and "Native"
according to the TDX spec.

Co-developed-by: Isaku Yamahata <isaku.yamahata@intel.com>
Signed-off-by: Isaku Yamahata <isaku.yamahata@intel.com>
Signed-off-by: Sagi Shahar <sagis@google.com>
Signed-off-by: Ackerley Tng <ackerleytng@google.com>
Signed-off-by: Ryan Afranji <afranji@google.com>
---
- Yan: rebased to tdx_kvm_dev-2024-06-21

- Reinette: Squash fix from Isaku to update verify_td_cpuid() fma check.
  First ensure that CPUID entries used in comparison are those the
  vCPU was initialized with after making TDX adjustments and then
  guest cpuid.1.ecx[12] can be checked with value of cpuid passed to
  KVM_TDX_INIT_VM. Give attribution.

- Reinette: Remove "Change-Id:" tag.

- Reinette: checkpatch.pl fixes: lines should not end with a '(',
  alignment should match open parenthesis.

- Reinette: remove '/**' kerneldoc marker from comment that does
  not follow kerneldoc syntax.

- Reinette: switch to reverse fir where practical

- Reinette: Drop CPUID filtering since kvm_vcpu->cpuid bits are more
  accurate with update to use KVM_TDX_GET_CPUID as baseline that already
  reflects filtering.
