From e36633eebdbbf63fdabda0cdb65a2ffc8dafebc2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roger Wang <runanwang@google.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Jun 2024 01:40:04 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 89/98] KVM: selftests: TDX: Add TDG.VP.INFO test

Adds a test for TDG.VP.INFO

Signed-off-by: Roger Wang <runanwang@google.com>
Signed-off-by: Sagi Shahar <sagis@google.com>
Signed-off-by: Ackerley Tng <ackerleytng@google.com>
Signed-off-by: Ryan Afranji <afranji@google.com>
---
- Reinette: Squash fix from Isaku to drop the unused
  TDX_TDPARAM_ATTR_PKS_BIT attribute. No attribution for small change.
- Reinette: Squash fix from Isaky to add a test for arch.s_bit that was
  exported to guest. No attribution for small change.
- Reinette: Squash fix from Rick to fix the hardcoded max vCPUs. No
  attribution for small change.
- Reinette: Remove "Change-Id:" tag.
- Reinette: Squash fix from Adrian that sets shared bit position based
  on guest maximum physical address width instead of maximum physical
  address width, because that is what KVM uses, refer to
  setup_tdparams_eptp_controls(), and because maximum physical address
  width can be different.
- Reinette: checkpatch.pl fix: alignment should match open parenthesis,
  prefer using the BIT macro
- Reinette: switch to reverse fir where practical
- Reinette: Use vcpu_get_cpuid_entry() to avoid stale data per commit
  "KVM: selftests: Refresh vCPU CPUID cache in __vcpu_get_cpuid_entry()".
  Use vCPU's CPUID bits after after switch to use KVM_TDX_GET_CPUID as
  baseline.
---
 .../selftests/kvm/include/x86/tdx/tdcall.h    |  19 +++
 .../selftests/kvm/include/x86/tdx/tdx.h       |   5 +
 .../selftests/kvm/lib/x86/tdx/tdcall.S        |  68 ++++++++
 tools/testing/selftests/kvm/lib/x86/tdx/tdx.c |  27 ++++
